/* Age-band sagas. Every age group has its own story, villain, zone names and 100 level names.
   Band 1 = age 4, band 2 = age 5, band 3 = age 6, band 4 = age 7.
   v26: the four sagas were rewritten as connected stories, one chapter per zone, so a child feels the journey move on:
     age 4  The Little Knight's Wonder Book: a little knight fills a book with the wonder of each land (Puff the grumpy cloud).
     age 5  The Lone Knight and the Star of Tomorrow: a knight with an empty shield learns who they are and brightens the future (Momo).
     age 6  The Young Knight Who Would Be King: ten Royal Trials prove the knight is fit to wear the crown (Murk, a rival).
     age 7  The Ten Star Seals: a young knight relights ten seals to lock away the giant demon Drakmor.
   Zone: [nameEN, nameMS, emoji, problemEmoji, fixedEmoji, hue, night, particle, 'ten EN level names', 'ten MS level names',
          story (6 shots [EN, MS]), boss intro (3 shots [EN, MS]), victory {fix, next} ([EN, MS] each)]
   Story shots follow the camera plan in 16-bosses-steam-comics.js: zone 5 shots 3-4 and zone 10 shot 3 show the villain,
   and zone 10 shot 6 is the finale. {hero} is the player's hero name, {boss} the boss monster, {next} the next zone.
   Band fields: vsad = [villain sad in zone 5, villain sad in zone 10], vfin = villain shown beaten in the finale,
   prog = [icon, EN, MS] progress line on the map, beat = victory line after any zone boss, fin = the saga's last line. */
const Z = (n, m, em, bad, good, hue, night, part, lv, lvm, story, boss, vict) => ({ n: [n, m], em, bad, good, hue, night, part, lv: lv.split('|').map((x, i) => [x, lvm.split('|')[i]]), story, boss, vict });

